r the picture above. Which of the following is a unit vector that is parallel to $q + r$?"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186097177 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8688d259-91a0-57b9-a118-ec71feec2112" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{65}}c" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095036} {:answer/id #uuid "a1324d04-e706-5a76-a501-88a91adb3e11" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{55}}c" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095037} {:answer/id #uuid "228bdee3-07e5-5a7d-9a23-1d3da2c66da2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{65}}{4}c" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095038} {:answer/id #uuid "44ddca2e-c35f-567f-9191-68cb552e7650" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{55}}c" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095039} {:answer/id #uuid "4741a424-03b7-5a24-97e3-1e5c43226795" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{65}}c" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095040}] :answer-field/id #uuid "943eaa96-2961-5fec-9654-295f42c3d887" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095035}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "8ddbfd9c-fd49-551e-8c5c-9bdbb0fc04fb" :question/math-academy-id "q-20407" :question/problem "![](images/13/1319298a994d5daf26853baf7d255490827ada4123debdf0b4374db1ed03f7af.png)\n\nConsider the picture shown above. Find a unit vector that is parallel to $c$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105488 :question/id #uuid "1a24b403-754c-5424-8182-8cad3487deed" :question/math-academy-id "e-15606" :question/problem "Suppose $|\\,\\mathbf{a}\\,|=13$ and the angle between vectors $\\mathbf{a}$ and $\\mathbf{b}$ is $\\theta = \\dfrac{2\\pi}{3}.$ Find the scalar projection of $\\mathbf{a}$ onto $\\mathbf{b}.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the formula for the scalar projection, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{comp}}_{b}\\,a & =|\\,a\\,|\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =13\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{2\\pi }{3}\\right) \\\\  & =13\\cdot \\left(-\\frac{1}{2}\\right) \\\\  & =-\\frac{13}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105489 :question/id #uuid "da8a1521-86cc-5747-88a7-e2ec56010c11" :question/math-academy-id "e-15607" :question/problem "Let $\\mathbf{a}=\\langle 3,3,-1 \\rangle$ and $\\mathbf{b}=\\langle 2,-7,0 \\rangle.$ Find the scalar projection of $\\mathbf{a}$ onto $\\mathbf{b}.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the formula for the scalar projection, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{comp}}_{b}\\,a & =\\frac{a\\cdot b}{|\\,b\\,|} \\\\  & =\\frac{{a}_{x}{b}_{x}+{a}_{y}{b}_{y}+{a}_{z}{b}_{z}}{\\sqrt{{b}_{x}^{2}+{b}_{y}^{2}+{b}_{z}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{3\\cdot 2+3\\cdot (-7)+(-1)\\cdot 0}{\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+(-7)^{2}+{0}^{2}}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{15}{\\sqrt{53}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105490 :question/id #uuid "4693b28f-df75-574e-8e49-bb89e162b107" :question/math-academy-id "e-15608" :question/problem "Let $\\mathbf{a}={\\left[ \\begin{array}{c}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{array} \\right]}$ and $\\mathbf{b}={\\left[ \\begin{array}{c}2 \\\\ - 4 \\\\ 0\\end{array} \\right]}.$ Find the scalar projection of $\\mathbf{a}$ onto $\\mathbf{b}.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the formula for the scalar projection, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{comp}}_{b}\\,a & =\\frac{a\\cdot b}{|\\,b\\,|} \\\\  & =\\frac{{a}_{x}{b}_{x}+{a}_{y}{b}_{y}+{c}_{z}{b}_{z}}{\\sqrt{{b}_{x}^{2}+{b}_{y}^{2}+{b}_{z}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{0\\cdot 2+0\\cdot (-4)+1\\cdot 0}{\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+(-4)^{2}+{0}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{0}{\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+(-4)^{2}+{0}^{2}}} \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105590 :question/id #uuid "957d070a-edc8-521f-a5bd-d10177a0bdbc" :question/math-academy-id "e-4344" :question/problem "Calculate the area of the triangle spanned by $\\mathbf{a}=\\langle 4,0,-3 \\rangle$ and $\\mathbf{b}=\\langle 5,-1,2 \\rangle.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the formula, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\times b & =\\begin{vmatrix}i & j & k \\\\ 4 & 0 & -3 \\\\ 5 & -1 & 2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}0 & -3 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{vmatrix}i-\\begin{vmatrix}4 & -3 \\\\ 5 & 2\\end{vmatrix}j+\\begin{vmatrix}4 & 0 \\\\ 5 & -1\\end{vmatrix}k \\\\  & =(0\\cdot 2-(-3)\\cdot (-1))i-(4\\cdot 2-(-3)\\cdot 5)j+(4\\cdot (-1)-0\\cdot 5)k \\\\  & =-3i-23j-4k \\\\  & =⟨-3,-23,-4⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of the corresponding parallelogram is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =|\\,a\\times b\\,| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-3)^{2}+(-23)^{2}+(-4)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{554}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe area of the triangle is half of the area of the respective parallelogram. So, the area of the triangle is\n\n$$\nA_{\\triangle} = \\dfrac{1}{2}A = \\dfrac{\\sqrt{554}}{2}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105591 :question/id #uuid "e354c43b-837f-5447-9759-6aeb3952cd57" :question/math-academy-id "e-4345" :question/problem "Calculate the area of the $\\bigtriangleup\\!ABC,$ if $A(1,0,-2),$ $B(-2,0,1),$ $C(1,1,-1).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the vectors $\\overrightarrow{AB}$ and $\\overrightarrow{AC}\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =b-a \\\\  & =(-2i+k)-(i-2k) \\\\  & =-3i+3k \\\\  & =⟨-3,0,3⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =c-a \\\\  & =(i+j-k)-(i-2k) \\\\  & =j+k \\\\  & =⟨0,1,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the formula to compute the cross product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\times \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =\\begin{vmatrix}i & j & k \\\\ -3 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{vmatrix}i-\\begin{vmatrix}-3 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{vmatrix}j+\\begin{vmatrix}-3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{vmatrix}k \\\\  & =(0\\cdot 1-3\\cdot 1)i-(-3\\cdot 1-3\\cdot 0)j+(-3\\cdot 1-0\\cdot 0)k \\\\  & =-3i+3j-3k \\\\  & =⟨-3,3,-3⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of the parallelogram spanned by $\\overrightarrow{AB}$ and $\\overrightarrow{AC}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =|\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\times \\overset{\\to }{AC}| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-3)^{2}+{3}^{2}+(-3)^{2}} \\\\  & =3\\sqrt{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the area of the triangle is half of the area of the respective parallelogram. So, the area of $\\bigtriangleup\\!ABC$ is\n\n$$\nA_{\\bigtriangleup} = \\dfrac{1}{2}A = \\dfrac{3\\sqrt{3}}{2}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105592 :question/id #uuid "23793048-621c-5ab3-97ac-7e635553c947" :question/math-academy-id "e-4346" :question/problem "Calculate the length of the altitude $CH$ of the $\\bigtriangleup\\!ABC$ if $A(-1,1,0),$ $B(1,1,2),$ $C(1,-1,1).$" :question/worked-solution "Note that the length of the altitude (height) can be related to the area of the triangle as follows:\n\n$$\nA_{\\bigtriangleup} = \\dfrac{b \\cdot h}{2},\n$$\n\n \nwhere $b$ is a base and $h$ is the corresponding altitude of the triangle.\n\nFor the $\\bigtriangleup\\!ABC,$ we have $h=CH,$ and $b=AB.$ So, we have\n\n$$\nA_{\\bigtriangleup} = \\dfrac{1}{2} CH \\cdot AB.\n$$\n\nSo, to find $CH,$ we first find $A_{\\bigtriangleup}.$ To start, we find the vectors $\\overrightarrow{AB}$ and $\\overrightarrow{AC}\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =b-a \\\\  & =(i+j+2k)-(-i+j) \\\\  & =2i+2k \\\\  & =⟨2,0,2⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =c-a \\\\  & =(i-j+k)-(-i+j) \\\\  & =2i-2j+k \\\\  & =⟨2,-2,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\times \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =\\begin{vmatrix}i & j & k \\\\ 2 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -2 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{vmatrix}i-\\begin{vmatrix}2 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{vmatrix}j+\\begin{vmatrix}2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -2\\end{vmatrix}k \\\\  & =(0\\cdot 1-2\\cdot (-2))i-(2\\cdot 1-2\\cdot 2)j+(2\\cdot (-2)-0\\cdot 2)k \\\\  & =4i+2j-4k \\\\  & =⟨4,2,-4⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of the parallelogram spanned by $\\overrightarrow{AB}$ and $\\overrightarrow{AC}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =|\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\times \\overset{\\to }{AC}| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{4}^{2}+{2}^{2}+(-4)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{36} \\\\  & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe area of the triangle is half of the area of the respective parallelogram. So, the area of $\\bigtriangleup\\!ABC$ is\n\n$$\nA_{\\bigtriangleup} = \\dfrac{1}{2}A = \\dfrac{1}{2} \\cdot 6 = 3.\n$$\n\nLet's also compute $AB$ since it appears in the formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB & =|\\overset{\\to }{AB}| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+{0}^{2}+{2}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{8} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally, using the formula $A_{\\bigtriangleup} = \\dfrac{1}{2} CH \\cdot AB,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{△} & =\\frac{1}{2}CH\\cdot AB \\\\ 3 & =\\frac{1}{2}CH\\cdot 2\\sqrt{2} \\\\ 3 & =CH\\cdot \\sqrt{2} \\\\ CH & =\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ CH & =\\frac{3\\sqrt{2}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186106038 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8b24cdda-6887-539c-aa19-1c06e9321c24" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186102115} {:answer/id #uuid "d18d3c58-289e-5a20-94fe-dbe96e805c83" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186102116} {:answer/id #uuid "d9720da9-28f2-56fb-a1f5-59662d9ad0ce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186102117} {:answer/id #uuid "0dfd980b-6168-5088-a700-0e0079b992e9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186102118} {:answer/id #uuid "27950d87-f67f-542d-91b8-ca59d3df0945" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{8}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186102119}] :answer-field/id #uuid "9895968c-daeb-5a4a-ad5b-4bce722f55b1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186102114}] :question/id #uuid "1ea6d0bd-3f53-5b68-921a-856b3d897bbb" :question/math-academy-id "q-126501" :question/problem "Let $c = ⟨2, 1, 2⟩$ and $d = ⟨ - 1, 2, 2⟩$. Find $comp_{d}c + comp_{c}d$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186106098 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "38804ecb-a9e5-5292-83cd-22d2f3dddc02" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285314} {:answer/id #uuid "87af4911-57b8-5d1b-a61c-48885ecb8443" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286030} {:answer/id #uuid "b25bb67f-9d56-52b5-a4e4-2d21207798bb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}-1}{2\\sqrt{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286419} {:answer/id #uuid "b647e886-213b-5e34-8574-a0e95f37c1c8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286452} {:answer/id #uuid "db777d82-845a-5914-94e9-dcb99836452f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}-1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286786}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186286786} :answer-field/id #uuid "cc839666-75c3-59d3-a3a7-4e1a2451ad41" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287571}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "1e48bd53-4841-5a1d-adee-85eb3b590727" :question/math-academy-id "q-18374" :question/problem "Let $p=⟨\\sqrt{2},1,-1⟩$ and $q=⟨\\sqrt{8},-\\sqrt{3},1⟩.$ Find the scalar projection of $p$ onto $q.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the formula for the scalar projection, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{comp}}_{q}\\,p & =\\frac{p\\cdot q}{|\\,q\\,|} \\\\  & =\\frac{{p}_{x}{q}_{x}+{p}_{y}{q}_{y}+{p}_{z}{q}_{z}}{\\sqrt{{q}_{x}^{2}+{q}_{y}^{2}+{q}_{z}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}\\cdot \\sqrt{8}+1\\cdot (-\\sqrt{3})+(-1)\\cdot 1}{\\sqrt{(\\sqrt{8})^{2}+(-\\sqrt{3})^{2}+{1}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{3-\\sqrt{3}}{\\sqrt{12}} \\\\  & =\\frac{3-\\sqrt{3}}{2\\sqrt{3}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}-1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186106110 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ab7f1702-1411-5fe5-a8ea-1636ef34a764" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186102537} {:answer/id #uuid "c1388b85-6047-59c9-a0bd-3754ff85c316" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186102538} {:answer/id #uuid "c66e78e6-af65-5cfd-90e1-b0cdc12cceeb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "7\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186102539} {:answer/id #uuid "2680133c-34ee-54a8-8c54-68017a6c0a70" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186102540} {:answer/id #uuid "41a13b60-bbd5-5c30-aa07-28737f3e5ba3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186102541}] :answer-field/id #uuid "62aa4579-02fb-5f2e-b93a-28a0e8d8c192" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186102536}] :question/id #uuid "13abcc9b-d205-521b-b9f3-45f8e21bde00" :question/math-academy-id "q-19136" :question/problem "Suppose $\\mid c|= 14$ and the angle between vectors $c$ and $d$ is $θ = 60^{∘}$. Find the scalar projection of $c$ onto $d$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186106120 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2513eb07-16be-5286-bc33-d8aa8c46c1cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{273}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285112} {:answer/id #uuid "66423ab8-fae7-5127-a7c3-1cdcd20b4cdf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{285}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285714} {:answer/id #uuid "6eb9250a-2aa6-5790-8265-790a777b83b3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{825}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285813} {:answer/id #uuid "d4231ebb-ea19-5c2a-a034-0b7b57f48b39" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\sqrt{177}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286716} {:answer/id #uuid "d4b9c672-c12b-55d0-930a-778da5483675" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{582}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286720}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186285714} :answer-field/id #uuid "ac35f525-4afb-57b4-9fa8-5e8beb00c4c3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287501}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "9432694c-4fbd-5497-812b-7bbf4e4f27ac" :question/math-academy-id "q-19983" :question/problem "Calculate the area of the triangle spanned by $a=⟨1,3,2⟩$ and $b=⟨4,1,-2⟩.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the formula, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\times b & =\\begin{vmatrix}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 1 & -2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}3 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{vmatrix}i-\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ 4 & -2\\end{vmatrix}j+\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 3 \\\\ 4 & 1\\end{vmatrix}k \\\\  & =(3\\cdot (-2)-1\\cdot 2)i-(1\\cdot (-2)-4\\cdot 2)j+(1\\cdot 1-4\\cdot 3)k \\\\  & =-8i+10j-11k \\\\  & =⟨-8,10,-11⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of the corresponding parallelogram is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =|\\,a\\times b\\,| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-8)^{2}+{10}^{2}+(-11)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{285}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe area of the triangle is half of the area of the respective parallelogram. So, the area of the triangle is\n\n$$\n{A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}A=\\frac{\\sqrt{285}}{2}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186106121 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8ac7131d-bfd4-5f3e-bab3-45391fafe62f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{3\\sqrt{3}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186102603} {:answer/id #uuid "b7e95b0b-62a1-5619-b9ab-2516eedd3655" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\fra